------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1a. jmdict-seed.sqlite
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two upstream works, both CC BY-SA 4.0, are combined in this one file.

JMdict, the Japanese/English dictionary:

  Copyright (c) James William Breen and The Electronic Dictionary Research and Development
  Group (EDRDG), Monash University.
  Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
  Project:  https://www.edrdg.org/jmdict/j_jmdict.html
  Licence:  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  Source file: JMdict_e.gz from https://ftp.edrdg.org/pub/Nihongo/JMdict_e.gz

JmdictFurigana, the per-kanji ruby segmentation of JMdict entries:

  Copyright (c) Doublevil and the JmdictFurigana contributors.
  The DATA is derived from JMdict and KANJIDIC and is distributed under the same CC BY-SA
  terms as JMdict. The generator SOURCE is MIT, which does not apply to the rows embedded
  here: what ships is data, so the data licence is the one that governs.
  Project:  https://github.com/Doublevil/JmdictFurigana
  Release:  JmdictFurigana 2.3.1, the snapshot the `furigana` rows were verified against
            (recorded in `Tools/build-jmdict.swift`).

Snapshot. EDRDG republishes JMdict daily, so the snapshot matters. Both source files were
taken on 2025-08-21. JMdict's own creation date is carried in a comment at the head of the
XML, which is the authoritative identification of any copy you rebuild from.

Transformations applied. This is a DERIVED work, not a copy:

  - Only a curated subset ships. The full JMdict is roughly 66 MB; this seed is 28 KB, a few
    dozen common entries, and exists so a fresh checkout and a first launch have a working
    dictionary before anything is downloaded or built. Apps supply a full dictionary through
    `JMDictStore(databaseURL:)`.
  - The XML is converted to SQLite and denormalized for read-only lookup:
    `entry(id, senses_json)`, `entry_form(entry_id, form, is_kanji)` and
    `furigana(form, reading, segmentation)`. Senses become one JSON blob per entry.
  - Per-sense cross-references, dialects, information fields and non-English glosses are
    dropped. Nothing is added to or altered in the meanings that remain.
  - The JmdictFurigana rows are parsed from the upstream `kanji|reading|segmentation` line
    format into the `furigana` table, with malformed lines skipped.

Update procedure. `Tools/build-jmdict.swift` is the reproducible build, and it is what a
rebuild must go through so the result stays a documented transformation:

  1. Download `JMdict_e.gz` into `data/` from the URL above.
  2. Download `JmdictFurigana.txt` into `data/` from the JmdictFurigana releases page, or
     point `JMDICT_FURIGANA_PATH` at it.
  3. `swift Tools/build-jmdict.swift out.sqlite` builds the full dictionary (roughly 66 MB,
     for an app to ship or cache; it is not committed here).
     `swift Tools/build-jmdict.swift --seed out.sqlite` rebuilds the committed seed.
  4. Record the new snapshot date here, and the new JmdictFurigana release, whenever either
     source is refreshed. An attribution that names the wrong snapshot is a broken
     attribution.

