1b. kanjidic.sqlite
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

KANJIDIC2, the per-character kanji dictionary:

  Copyright (c) The Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group (EDRDG),
  Monash University.
  Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
  Project:  https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project
  Licence:  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  Source file: kanjidic2.xml.gz from https://www.edrdg.org/kanjidic/kanjidic2.xml.gz

Snapshot. The source file was taken on 2025-09-07. As with JMdict, EDRDG republishes it, and
the file's own header comment identifies the revision of any copy you rebuild from.

Transformations applied. Again a DERIVED work:

  - Filtered to roughly 3,100 of KANJIDIC2's roughly 13,000 characters: only those carrying a
    school grade, a frequency rank or an old-JLPT level. The rest are historical variants and
    personal-name characters a reader will not meet in a book. That filter is why this one
    file can ship whole at 332 KB while JMdict cannot.
  - Converted to SQLite as one read-only table:
    `kanji(character, on_readings, kun_readings, meanings, stroke_count, grade, frequency)`,
    with the three list columns as JSON arrays.
  - The thirty-odd per-character dictionary index numbers (Nelson, Halpern, Heisig,
    Morohashi and the rest), all non-English meanings, radical decompositions and codepoints
    are dropped. Readings and English meanings are carried through unaltered.

Update procedure. `Tools/build-kanjidic.swift`:

  1. Download `kanjidic2.xml.gz` into `data/` from the URL above.
  2. `swift Tools/build-kanjidic.swift Packages/KBDictionaryKit/Sources/KBDictionaryKit/Resources/kanjidic.sqlite`
  3. Record the new snapshot date here.

