1c. What a consuming app must do
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Linking `KBDictionaryKit` puts CC BY-SA 4.0 data inside your application bundle, so you
redistribute it. CC BY-SA 4.0 section 3(a) requires, in material that accompanies the
distribution:

  1. Credit the data in your About screen (or equivalent user-facing credits). Name JMdict
     and the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group with James Breen, name
     KANJIDIC2 and EDRDG, and name JmdictFurigana with Doublevil.
  2. State that the data is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 and include the licence text or a link to
     <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>.
  3. State that the data has been modified, and say how, or link to this file. The filtering
     and reshaping described above are modifications under the licence.
  4. Keep it separable from your own licence terms. The ShareAlike condition attaches to the
     DATA and to adaptations of it, not to your application code, which is why these files are
     carved out here rather than folded into the Apache-2.0 grant.


